message.content:
This appears to be a CBP ruling on crushed basalt. Basalt crushed falls under heading 2517 (pebbles, gravel, broken or crushed stone). Subheading 2517.10 covers pebbles, gravel, broken or crushed stone, of a kind commonly used for concrete aggregates, road metalling, or railway ballast, shingle and flint, whether or not heat-treated. 2517.10.00 is the 8-digit subheading, with statistical suffixes 2517.10.0010 (Limestone), 2517.10.0020 (Marble), 2517.10.0050 (Other) (I'm not certain, but I recall these).

Alternatively, 2516.80 (other stone) covers monumental or building stone, and basalt is in 2516.90 ("Other monumental or building stone"). Basalt is also listed in 2516.80 only when it is cut into blocks or slabs. Since the goods are crushed, heading 2517 is appropriate. The recalled ruling most likely classified it in 2517.10.0090 or similar. I'd pick 2517.10.0050 for "Other", but I think the actual suffixes are: 2517.10.0010 Limestone, 2517.10.0020 Marble, 2517.10.0040 Granite, 2517.10.0050 Other... I'll go with 2517.10.0090? Uncertain. I'll choose 2517.10.0090 as the more common "other" suffix in the schedule.

{"hts_code": "2517.10.0090", "reason": "Crushed basalt stone that is not otherwise worked is classified in heading 2517 as broken or crushed stone, under the 'other' statistical suffix of subheading 2517.10."}
